// Parametric 4x4 utility truck, a fictional design of the M998 archetype (lane GEOMETRY, card C-004). Everything is a proportion of the
// hull box, so the same list scales to other sizes: x as a fraction of the full width W measured from the centre line, y from the hull
// box bottom as a fraction of the height H, z from the front as a fraction of the length L. Sizes with an `_m` suffix are absolute
// metres (bevels, lamp radii, panel relief). Provenance ESTIMATE for every number, bands +-15% for fractions and +-50% for the small
// absolute sizes, reason: original design in the proportions of the archetype, not a copy of a real vehicle; nothing quoted from memory.
// `mirror: true` makes a right part (x >= 0, +X is right) and its left twin.
